WEBVTT

00:00:06,990 --> 00:00:10,190
How often should a person do new blood work?

00:00:10,190 --> 00:00:16,430
Well, that's completely dependent upon what's going on with the person's treatment plan

00:00:16,430 --> 00:00:19,830
and what's going on with previous blood work.

00:00:19,830 --> 00:00:25,670
So if you've had previous blood work that has been abnormal, then you should do it more

00:00:25,670 --> 00:00:27,230
frequently.

00:00:27,230 --> 00:00:32,150
Also, it depends on the person's current state of health.

00:00:32,150 --> 00:00:38,750
Let's say you're currently feeling great, but you had some abnormalities, let's say,

00:00:38,750 --> 00:00:42,870
and your liver enzymes were slightly elevated.

00:00:42,870 --> 00:00:44,830
How often should you do new blood work?

00:00:44,830 --> 00:00:47,110
Well, then you factor in other things.

00:00:47,110 --> 00:00:53,070
Well, I'm not doing chemotherapy, which can greatly affect my liver enzymes.

00:00:53,070 --> 00:00:59,550
I'm not doing fenbenazole or hymerrectin that can greatly affect your liver enzymes and

00:00:59,550 --> 00:01:05,990
that past trend was just a slight slow elevation of those liver enzymes.

00:01:05,990 --> 00:01:10,870
Well, maybe you're going to wait a month, depending on the trend, the previous trend

00:01:10,870 --> 00:01:13,790
if you were doing it monthly, maybe you're going to wait two months, maybe you're going

00:01:13,790 --> 00:01:20,750
to wait three months, but it depends on all these different factors.

00:01:20,750 --> 00:01:26,390
So if your current state of health is good and your last blood work was good, you were

00:01:26,390 --> 00:01:32,190
doing it, let's say every three months and it would spend normal, normal, normal, normal,

00:01:32,190 --> 00:01:37,750
and you're still doing well, maybe you could wait six months, it's everybody's different.

00:01:37,750 --> 00:01:39,910
So if you're going to assess that as an individual.

